{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T07:39:36.176Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0f4588e252f0b0333b54fb6b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T07:39:36.175Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Reproduced the blocking re-review finding in a disposable fixture repository. With core.autocrlf=true, the staged writer materializes the frozen tree with git read-tree -u (a checkout), so LF blobs are smudged to CRLF before bundling: the committed bundle then fails accept:self-host on a default (no-conversion) checkout of the same commit. The same rule is violated on the consumer side: git worktree add extraction in the verify path converts committed LF to CRLF, so a correct bundle fails accept:self-host whenever the host enables conversion. Both fail closed today; the fix is to read raw blob bytes from the git object database (ls-tree plus cat-file, which never apply filters) on both the staged-write and verify paths."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T07:39:36.176Z"}],"before_hash":"1550f2357b40bd66274085347edf93348faf559c217ca51daccc8a79d7227c61","after_hash":"b7d759e25c34e017e9f62a081ca5fe0a9efa779c3627bf78bed34690be38f921","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fb1ea5b7a7cf6871cc778cc36466ac61a7e2bbe12ec339ca4cd1e3861b856ee8"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T08:19:39.360Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0f4588e252f0b0333b54fb6b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T08:19:39.359Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Fix for the blocking finding: the staged writer and the verifier now read git content straight from the object database. writeStagedSnapshot freezes the index with git write-tree, then a new readTreeSnapshot lists the frozen tree (ls-tree -r -z, NUL-delimited) and reads every blob raw through one cat-file --batch process; the configuration is parsed from the staged tree's own self-host.json bytes. The verify path reads HEAD the same way, replacing the git worktree extraction, which applied checkout conversions on conversion-enabled hosts and failed clean repositories. General rule violated by the finding: a byte-exact archive contract must never materialize content through a checkout, because checkout applies core.autocrlf, eol attributes and filter drivers. Searched the package for the class: the staged writer (read-tree -u) and the verify extraction (worktree add) were the only two materialization sites; every other git read already goes through cat-file (raw). File modes now come from the tree instead of the filesystem, gitlinks are refused loudly at listing, and tracked symlinks keep their historical bundle bytes (target text, non-executable)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T08:19:39.360Z"}],"before_hash":"b7d759e25c34e017e9f62a081ca5fe0a9efa779c3627bf78bed34690be38f921","after_hash":"1bd756237b82d5310ad6c2795400d2a261244fb5b5ef8885809301ac24592688","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4a34a9728ca5a56dc8cdab8b40960ea31c8c35820eb1eab93919df539f5ddbd3"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T08:19:44.312Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0f4588e252f0b0333b54fb6b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T08:19:44.312Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Revert proof (disposable copy, restored by disposal): with readTreeSnapshot behaviorally reverted to a checkout-based materialization (read-tree --reset -u into a scratch work-tree) while keeping the new tests and exports, all four conversion tests fail (0 of 4): the staged writer under core.autocrlf=true bundles 16 CRLF bytes where the tree stores 14 LF bytes, the per-path byte-equality property fails, the conversion-enabled accept fails a clean repository, and the raw committed-bytes unit test fails its content comparison. With the fix in place the same file passes 74 of 74 (Node, focused run). The class search also covered the legacy working-tree writer mode, the caller workflows (they invoke the same writer), the release and dependency-refresh hooks, and non-git trackers (the gate refuses a missing repository); no other instance exists."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T08:19:44.312Z"}],"before_hash":"1bd756237b82d5310ad6c2795400d2a261244fb5b5ef8885809301ac24592688","after_hash":"112810d35045a811afe733f551dd8f6cb3b6345f3856d13a1992d0b83878024b","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b00dab8125eceae3e969de5369a288d4eec63bc8417270572fb03bbbedcd088b"}
