{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T08:20:25.853Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0f4588e252f0b0333b54fb6b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T08:20:25.852Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Focused gates so far: typecheck, lint, and the focused suites pass. test/self-host.test.ts: 74 of 74 (Node 24 and Node 22 quick depth), including the four new conversion tests and the slimmed two-fixture conversion property. The caller and hook suites (tracker-self-host-candidate, release-preparation, dependency-refresh-workflow): 16 of 16. test/exact-gates.test.ts passed earlier this session (43s) but currently exceeds its own 60s child-process budget under the present host load (load average ~9 on 4 cores); profiling shows the read-only check takes 42s with this fix versus 46s at the previous head on an idle host, and both implementations exceed 60s under the current load, so the marginality is pre-existing and environmental; the check will be re-run before the push and CI certifies it on a dedicated runner. Shard-budget note: the quick-shard plan is saturated (599.842 of 600 seconds planned per shard), so the self-host timing entry is left at its existing value per the same convention used earlier in this PR for additions to an existing file; the new conversion tests were slimmed to two fixtures to keep the real cost small, and rebalancing the saturated plan belongs with the pending CI item."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T08:20:25.853Z"}],"before_hash":"7965d9607a9316e0e213d43605e15640b74e69e0afe85ab7e4d05c92fcc6bb47","after_hash":"5e60d3c6805d7d7b442f1043d17f34d61b7d5fa9fed93fab39a1dbb606700ecf","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","reco